          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP241 Edmonton Kensington village 

Out with the kids to find a few caps on this beautiful day.TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684645454">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="53.592000" lon="-113.540967" />
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="11091667">WillowZilla</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP241 - Edmonton - Kensington Village&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Another nicely dug out and cleaned cap, almost like someone has been here recently!  Nice readable numbers as well.  Kind of exposed location so was nice to not have to stay there too long.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684116952">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-05T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP241 Edmonton - Kensington Village&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time for a couple more caps in the area after 'capping out' St. Albert.  I was basically heading in the right direction for home but I figured I could grab these up quick.  Not overly quick but still findable.  This one had a bit of a layer of mud and dirt on it but the hole was still pretty defined.  I got what I came for and then headed back to my car parked in the lot across the street.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enjoying these caps. Sure wish I had discovered them earlier in our caching career.  TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
